From 6e9d1ac71bfa0de9e065c198586ec052781e5a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:37:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-14: compare with DFM / reset to DFM value in the
 property grid (0.14.0)

WPF "Reset Value": every editable property shows the BCB6 .dfm value beside it;
a row whose page value differs is marked and gets a reset button that writes the
DFM value back (one undo step, like any other edit).

- lib/format.js dfmEditValues(node): only what the DFM actually says (a default
  or ParentFont property stays null, not guessed); the & accelerator is dropped
  from Caption; a system colour (clBtnFace ...) is given by name only -- its RGB
  is the Windows theme's, so it is not compared (5,268 of 14,641 colours in the IR).
- Font.Name counts as the same when the page's font list names the DFM font
  (the pages use "Microsoft JhengHei","MS Sans Serif" on purpose); the probe now
  reports the whole family list.
- Measured over all pages: position/size equal to the DFM 12,228, different 432
  (mostly pop-up panels the web author moved on purpose).
- vscode_it.ps1 -AllPages also sweeps web\*.html: 128 pass / 0 fail, all files
  MD5-unchanged (background.html, boot_wait.html, pci1203.html included).

Tests: lib 91, probe, smoke 54, panels (Font.Size / Font.Bold exactly the marked
rows on spbSave, reset posts fontSize=16), real VS Code 55 -- all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
